# .NET Common Native API

The host binds a tenant once with
`EngineQueryContext.Configure(domain, adapter).WithTenant(8)`. The domain owns
`source.tenant_field`; fluent writes omit the matching tenant assignment, while
reads, actions and transaction callbacks retain it.

This notebook runs the committed C# sample against an in-memory SQLite database.
It requires the .NET SDK selected by `selecto-dotnet/global.json` and `mise` on
PATH. It creates no persistent database. Set `SELECTO_DOTNET_PATH` when the native
checkout is not a sibling of `selecto_livebooks`. The verified native revision is
`f312f91` (see the native migration audit for the full source snapshot).

## Inspect the native C# program

```elixir
repo = System.get_env("SELECTO_DOTNET_PATH") || Path.expand("../../selecto-dotnet", __DIR__)
source = Path.join(repo, "examples/CommonNativeApi/Program.cs")
IO.puts(File.read!(source))
```

The sample supplies a real domain, previews SQL with separate parameters,
inserts without `org_id`, invokes the domain's archive action in a transaction,
and verifies that a refused foreign-row delete rolls back an earlier insert.
The final scoped read sees only the committed tenant's archived row.

## Execute and verify

```elixir
mise = System.find_executable("mise") || raise "mise executable is required"
{output, status} = System.cmd(mise, ["exec", "--", "dotnet", "run", "--project", "examples/CommonNativeApi", "--configuration", "Release"], cd: repo, stderr_to_stdout: true)
IO.puts(output)
if status != 0 or not String.contains?(output, "PASS common native API:"), do: raise "Native C# sample failed"
```

For broader regression coverage, run `mise exec -- dotnet test --configuration
Release` in the native checkout. PostgreSQL integration checks additionally
require a disposable `SELECTO_CERT_DOTNET_POSTGRESQL_URL`. These checks do not
claim live coverage of every other adapter or arbitrary host action executor.
